> find it much problem.  I mean it takes a few turn longer and maybe I
> miss a potion or so in some corner, but whatever potion that is it's
> probably worth less than what I might wish for from the lamp.

If you're exploring a mines level without any light source you
have to take a lot more steps. You have to follow the perimeter
closely, and then walk across the open areas to see what's inside
them. This gives you more chances to walk over a game-crippling trap,
and means you will have to face more generated monsters. There
are lots of other little ways that it helps such as being able to
track your pets and their nearby mishaps.

I think there is room in the game for a wishable light source, as
long as it is not as good as a magic lamp. Candle radius and/or
flickers and/or long but not infinite duration, etc.

